NOTE: This licence covers this source code only.

Pretrained models downloaded by the optional neural backends carry their own
licences -- the XTTS-v2 checkpoint, for example, is released under the Coqui
Public Model License and does not permit commercial use.

The shipped reference statistics in voxprint/data/reference_dsp_v1.npz are
derived in part from the LibriSpeech corpus (dev-other), which is licensed
CC BY 4.0:

    V. Panayotov, G. Chen, D. Povey and S. Khudanpur, "LibriSpeech: an ASR
    corpus based on public domain audio books", ICASSP 2015.
    https://www.openslr.org/12/

The file contains two 373-element vectors of per-dimension means and standard
deviations computed over that corpus and over procedurally generated voices. It
contains no audio and nothing that identifies a speaker. Rebuild it from any
other corpus with tools/build_reference.py.
